  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding of Alaska Medicaid Gralise / Horizant criteria. Gralise (gabapentin ER) 300/600 mg: PHN only. Horizant (gabapentin enacarbil) 300/600 mg: PHN and primary RLS in adults.",
    "Approval paths retain diagnosis and product gates across all treatment alternatives. RLS also requires dose \u2264600 mg. Trial facts attest to adequate duration and, for gabapentin, dose; no additional trial-failure requirement is imposed. Contraindication facts include the clinically adverse event resulting from use. Denial text is interpreted as the mirror of these approval paths.",
    "Cautions (notes only): not interchangeable with other gabapentin products; may increase suicidal thoughts or behaviors; renal impairment may require dose adjustment.",
    "Authorization (notes only): initial approval up to 6 months; reauthorization up to 12 months with reported improvement.",
    "Quantity limits (notes only): Gralise maximum 1800 mg/day, 30 \u00d7 300 mg or 90 \u00d7 600 mg tablets/month; Horizant maximum 1200 mg/day, 30 \u00d7 300 mg or 60 \u00d7 600 mg tablets/month. Source quantities retained as written. The RLS-specific \u2264600 mg dose is encoded separately.",
    "Version 1; PDF Original 9/04/2018, Approval 9/21/2018. Archived effective_date 2018-01-01 retained; it is not a stated PDF effective date."
  ],
